{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/829618-compact-grimms-fairies-hunters","id":829618,"title":"[Compact?] Grimms - Fairies Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-14T02:11:40-08:00","id":829618,"title":"[Compact?] Grimms - Fairies Hunters","content":"So I starting to watch TV series <b>Grimm</b> and it's looks like ideal example of fairies ( like changelings or hobgoblins ) hunters. In the nutshell, Grimms are mortals having supernatural scenes to see Wesen ( fey ) creture. ( Seeing past the Mask, I assume. )<br /> <br /> Some history from <a href=\"http://grimm.wikia.com/wiki/Grimm\" target=\"_blank\">series Wikia</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Grimm Wikia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The D\u0113capit\u0101re (Lat. &quot;one who decapitates&quot;) were the earliest known Grimms, active in the first century AD.<br /> <br /> During the Fourth Crusade, seven knights in service to the Seven Houses participated in the sack of Constantinople. These knights were needed to keep the Wesen in line that made up the brunt of the Royals' Army. The knights brought back a treasure from Constantinople so powerful that they feared it coming into the possession of their masters. They hid the treasure and created a map in seven parts.<br /> <br /> The knights became the ancestors of what would come to be commonly known by the mid-1810s as Grimms (named after the The Brothers Grimm, who, ironically, did not inherit these traits from their ancestors and instead collected and recorded what they believed to be the mythologies of the world) .<br /> <br /> Over the next several centuries, the Grimms served as the (usually) freelance police of the Wesen world, dispatching those who could not live in peace with humans (by contrast, the Wesen Council enforced the internal rules of Wesen society). As a general rule, it was the responsibility of the Grimms to hunt down &quot;the bad ones,&quot; those aggressive and malicious Wesen who preyed on humans or other Wesen. The majority of Grimms were only exposed to the Wesen community through these malcontents, leading some of them, namely the Endezeichen Grimms, to consider all Wesen abominations that needed to be exterminated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great inspiration for the changeling Hunters. I'm also interested - <b>Would Grimms sight powers work as someking of hereditary Pledge? </b>It could work as interesting Endowment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-14-2016, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T02:21:37-08:00","id":829622,"title":"","content":"I actually am using Grimms as inspiration for a 'minor template' that's still in the works, which are basically lineages of supernaturally endowed hunters whose inherent abilities confer advantages against supernaturals that happen to be the favored enemies of their lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:00:57-08:00","id":829671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/829618-compact-grimms-fairies-hunters?p=829622#post829622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually am using Grimms as inspiration for a 'minor template' that's still in the works, which are basically lineages of supernaturally endowed hunters whose inherent abilities confer advantages against supernaturals that happen to be the favored enemies of their lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You understand you just described <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Heritage House group in the nutshell?<br /> <br /> Also, I would much rather see those as <b>HtV</b> open hunters - Grimms in <b>CoD</b> setting would have hands much more dirty with non </span></span>Wesen beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:05:31-08:00","id":829673,"title":"","content":"Yes. Yes, I did.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, I was thinking of revising the Heritage House as a compact comprised of those in that proposed template, though Striders <i>can</i> be found among other hunter groups. Still, if that doesn't work for you, that's fine.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:12:19-08:00","id":829781,"title":"","content":"One of my mom's drinking buddies is a descendant of one of the less famous Grimm brothers (the two that collected all the tales were the 2nd and 3rd eldest out of nine.). Given the weirdness in that circle of people, I can't help but think of Grimm's as being weirdness magnets as opposed to hunters. The laws of probability bend themselves into knots just to have Grimms encounter the supernatural and almost every close friend they have has a supernatural merit of some sort.<br /> <br /> This, combined with the fact that one of my special ed assistant people in middle school was a descendant of Fred Noonan (Earhart's navigator) makes me wonder if my hometown is some sort of god machine infrastructure designed to lure in people with family connections to high profile supernatural stuff, or a family history of supernatural merits, and keep them away from anything that might spark an interest in the supernatural. Said hometown recently was declared to be the 2nd most boring city in Georgia, so clearly it's working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:04:44-08:00","id":833272,"title":"","content":"Could be interesting. Could even expand it to other supernatual-hunting families, each who can &quot;see through&quot; one specific type of &quot;monster.&quot; The Compact/Conspiracy could be a loose affiliation of extended members of these families, pooling knowledge and resources for when, say, a Grimm meets a vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Van Helsings</b> can recognize Vampires on sight, perhaps see through their illusion powers. An extended family either descended from, or simply including, Abraham Van Helsing of Dracula.<br /> <br /> <b>Argents</b> can recognize Werewolves on sight in any form, and would be immune to Lunacy. Starting in France, the family includes Jean Chastel, the local man credited for killing the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_of_G%C3%A9vaudan\" target=\"_blank\">Beast of Gevaudan</a>. (Yes, I'm cribbing from Teen Wolf here. Seriously, it's awesome. And you can't get more on-point than a family of werewolf hunters named <i>Argent</i>.)<br /> <br /> <b>Shelleys</b> can see a Promethean's disfigurements, but suffer from Disquiet as any other. Interestingly, Shelleys do not typically hunt Prometheans, being fully aware of their tortured natures, and often try and help them on their Pilgrimages. They're quite prepared to deal with the ones who prove too dangerous, however.<br /> <br /> <b>Grimms</b> can see through a Changeling's Mask, and are one of the most contentious groups. Gimms seem to be split about fifty-fifty between those who believe that Changelings can be just as good or bad as anyone else, and those who believe the only good Changeling is a dead Changeling. If the Changelings fear anything as much as the True Fey, it is the Grimms. Which can make life for a Grimm who isn't interested in killing Changelings who haven't done anything wrong very interesting.<br /> <br /> (Not sure if Mages should have a dedicated Hunting family, and who they would be. Also don't know anything about game lines after Changeling, so don't feel qualified to speculate.)<br /> <br /> The way I would do their &quot;Sight&quot; is something like an Endowment, rated from one to five dots. Each dot lets them &quot;see&quot; their target creature through normal camouflage, or abilities at that dot rating or lower. For instance, a Van Helsing with one dot of &quot;Sight&quot; could recognize any vampire for what it is, and pierce any Obfuscate or other concealment/illusion Discipline power rated at one dot, though two-dot and higher abilities can still fool him. If you want to make it a little more fair for the monsters, simply have the &quot;Sight&quot; add to Clash of Wills rolls like Blood Potency, Primal Urge, et al., though this would make it difficult-to-impossible for these Hunters to detect very powerful members of their target species, which to my mind kind of defeats the purpose.<br /> <br /> When one of these Hunters uses their Sight to recognize their target monster, said monster also recognizes them for what they are (really liked the Grimm description of &quot;eyes going utterly black, seeing our true nature reflected back at us.&quot;) Again, this makes life for these hunters very interesting, since the monsters know that they know, and most of them aren't too comfortable with the idea of random mortals being able to see them for what they really are. Even a hunter only interested in killing the ones who deserve it will tend to engender fear, distrust, and hatred in their particular monster group. Many of these hunters have been unceremoniously killed the first time they saw their monster, because no one was around to tell them and prepare them for what to expect. The <i>really</i> dangerous ones had no idea, never had it explained to them, and <i>survived anyway</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}